PATCH 594: the trigonometry's carry and second lane -- 05dd/05e2's 1.0 flag, 03a9/0459/05b7/05bc
reading it, 0578's CX and a265's range word, 9a32's wind vector, b059's body.

board:0017.  Found by the seeded replay (patch 592) on AZER1, each verified against its asm:

  05dd, 05e2  the sine/cosine lookups return the 1.0 case in CF: `stc` on the two exits (the angle
              0x4000 exactly, and the interpolation carrying past 0xffff), `clc` (0x64a) otherwise --
              in particular when the interpolation lands on 0xffff without a carry (table[255] =
              0xffff with a fraction that rounds to 0).  The port had tested the VALUE for 0xffff and
              took the shortcut one LSB early: the player's hull velocity at heading 0x7fc9 came out
              -30 for the original's -29 (step 1738).
  03a9, 0459  `call 5e2 ; jb skip ; mul` -- each mul is skipped on that CARRY, now g_fist_cf.
  05b7, 05bc  `call 5e2 ; jb 5c4` -- the carry, not the `add ah,0x40` carry Ghidra kept (05b7) nor
              a dead local (05bc).
  0578, a265  0578 ends `pop cx ; mov bx,ax` with 0927's LOW word (the range) in CX; a265's
              `shl edx,8 ; mov dl,ch ; mov [di+0x99],dx` (0x1a2d6-0x1a2e3) builds the range in
              256-units from 0927's high word and that CH.  Patch 462 had taken CH from the height
              LUT word: every vehicle's range word sat at 0x07xx; the oracle's moves (step 101).
  9a32        the wind vector: `[0x92ee]=ax ; [0x92f0]=bx ; dx=bx ; call 3a9 ; movsx eax,ax ;
              [0x92f2]=eax ; movsx eax,dx ; [0x92f6]=eax` -- 03a9's TWO lanes sign-extended to
              dwords (9b11/9c4f add them to 32-bit positions).  Ghidra stored the raw magnitude as
              the y lane through a 16-bit accessor: every smoke child drifted +magnitude in y, never
              negative (step 1948).
  b059        at the asm's widths (0xb059-0xb0bd): `call b112 ; sub ax,[di+0x10]` a WORD bearing
              difference (`cmp ax,0x4000 ; jb ; cmp ax,0xc000 ; jb` = within +-90 degrees); `movsx
              eax,[di+0x59] ; shl eax,3` to dword[0x9962], the same for [di+0x5b] to dword[0x9966];
              with byte[di+0x45] set `mov dx,0x40 ; mov ax,[di+0x26] ; call 3a9` gives BOTH lanes;
              `lcall 0f69:b2a0 (a930) ; jae ; orw [di+0x40],8` sets bit 3 (the "blocked ahead" bit
              ae7b/af10 test) on a930's CARRY.  Ghidra read 32-bit words, stored 16 of the 32 result
              bits, took the magnitude 0x40 for the DX lane and folded the CF test to a constant
              (step 2358).

